WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.490
MINHAZ KAZI: Welcome
to DataVis DevTalk.

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:05.040
I'm your host, Minhaz
Kazi, developer advocate

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:06.840
for Data Studio.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:09.060
In this video, we'll talk
about community connectors

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:12.780
and how you can use them to
fetch your data in Data Studio.

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:13.530
Let's get started.

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:21.830
Data Studio helps you
to organize, access,

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:23.990
and understand your information.

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:26.000
Although different
individuals and businesses

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.950
have different
needs, it is often

00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:30.950
useful to have a comprehensive
view of their data.

00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:33.380
You might have data
from different sources,

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:37.340
social media, analytics,
advertising, et cetera.

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:39.510
You might also have
organizational data,

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:43.190
including sales, finance,
and human resource.

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:47.180
Your data can be hosted and
available in different places.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:49.200
You might have
on-premise private data.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.410
For example, you might
have marketing information

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:54.830
on a MySQL server on
your corporate network.

00:00:54.830 --> 00:00:56.930
You can have private
data on the cloud.

00:00:56.930 --> 00:01:00.840
Maybe you're using Firebase
database for your application.

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:03.020
You can also be using data
from commercial platforms

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:05.710
like Google Analytics
and Google Ads.

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:09.350
Another interesting use case
is using public data sets.

00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:11.950
A prime example of that is
the BigQuery public data

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:15.650
set which is available
for everyone to use.

00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:18.690
If you want to analyze
and visualize your data

00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:21.530
you'll need to connect to
your data in Data Studio,

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:24.350
and that's where
connectors come in.

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:27.140
Data Studio provides a
number of connectors for you

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:29.150
to connect to your own data.

00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:31.220
You can connect to
a GCP data source

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:35.720
like Sheets, BigQuery,
Cloud SQL, Cloud Storage,

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:37.670
and Cloud Spanner.

00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:39.590
You can connect to
different Google services

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:43.340
like Google Analytics,
Google Ads, Search Console,

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:47.224
YouTube Analytics,
Attribution 360, and more.

00:01:47.224 --> 00:01:49.140
There are also connectors
available to connect

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:52.940
to your own instances
of MySQL and PostgreSQL.

00:01:52.940 --> 00:01:55.780
But what if your data is
not in any of these sources

00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:57.950
and is in somewhere else?

00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:02.030
Well, in that case, you can
use community connectors.

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:04.070
Community connectors
are custom connectors

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:07.340
that you can create
using Apps Script.

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:10.560
Apps Script is Google's
scripting language.

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:12.890
It is a JavaScript
platform on the cloud.

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:16.320
You can access it by going
to script.google.com.

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:19.220
Apps Script lets you
do more with Google.

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:20.990
Using it, you can
increase the power

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:24.380
of all these Google
applications by using their API

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:26.777
and also by building
custom add-ons.

00:02:26.777 --> 00:02:28.610
So when you create your
own custom connector

00:02:28.610 --> 00:02:30.650
using Apps Script,
you can fetch data

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:32.720
from almost any
internet-accessible data

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:34.280
source.

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:38.930
You can use web API endpoints,
flash files like CSV, JSON,

00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:43.790
XML, databases with
JDBC APIs, and also

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:45.950
many Apps Script services.

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:47.510
In this video
series, we will show

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:51.410
you step by step how you can
build your own connector.

00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:53.210
Once you've built a
community connector,

00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:55.160
you can obviously
use it yourself

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:58.120
to bring in your own
data into Data Studio.

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:00.680
Now your co-worker sees
you using that connector

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:03.162
but thinks that it will
be useful for them.

00:03:03.162 --> 00:03:05.120
They don't have to build
it from scratch again.

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:08.750
You can just share your
connector with specific users.

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:11.450
After a certain time, several
people in your organization

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:15.200
start using your connector,
and it gets really popular.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:16.940
You can make it
securely available

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:18.740
within your organization.

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:21.680
That way, anyone in the
organization can use it,

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:25.100
but the access and the
data remain secure.

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:28.340
You can also make your
connector available to everyone.

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:30.020
And one of the
ways you can do it

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:32.510
is by publishing it to the
Data Studio Partner Connector

00:03:32.510 --> 00:03:33.870
Gallery.

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:35.930
There are more than 100
connectors available

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:39.320
that connect to over
500 data sources.

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:41.900
You can try out these partner
connectors by visiting

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:47.510
the gallery at
datastudio.google.com/data.

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:49.980
So that was an overview
of community connectors.

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:51.940
In our next video, we
will talk about how

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:53.640
community connectors work.

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:55.330
You can always go to
our developer site

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:58.720
at
developers.google.com/datastudio

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:01.150
for more information.

00:04:01.150 --> 00:04:03.520
If you enjoyed this
video, like and subscribe

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:06.230
to the GCB channel for
more videos like this.

00:04:06.230 --> 00:04:08.010
Thanks for watching.

